<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept industrial output rises 1 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept industrial output rises 1 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in September increased a preliminary 1.0 percent from the previous month on a seasonally adjusted basis, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>MITI said in a statement that industrial output was on a gradual upward trend.</p>
<p>Industrial production in the July-September period rose 1.5 percent from the previous quarter, it said.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the preliminary monthly figures follows:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month-on-month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>				  SEPT     MONTH AGO     SEPT INDEX</p>
<p> Output			 +1.0	-2.3	 97.3</p>
<p> Shipments		    +1.3	-2.3	 98.8</p>
<p> Inventories		  -1.0	+0.8	 107.6</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 -0.9	+1.3	 115.8</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year (in pct):</p>
<p>				   SEPT     MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			  +3.4	+1.8</p>
<p> Shipments		     +3.0	+1.3</p>
<p> Inventories		   +0.3	+1.6</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>    Shipments ratio	 -1.2	+0.4</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of MITI's forecasts for</p>
<p>manufacturers' output:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted, month-on-month (in pct):</p>
<p>		     OCT forecast   NOV forecast</p>
<p>		     +4.0	     -1.9</p>
